**A. Purpose.** Historic preservation incentives increase the potential for historic resources to be preserved, rehabilitated, and reused. Incentives make preservation and rehabilitation more attractive to tenants and owners of historic resources because they provide use flexibility and economic opportunities. Some incentives also allow for broader public access to certain historic resources.

**B. Eligibility for historic preservation incentives.** The following are eligible for historic resource incentives:

1. Historic Landmarks and Conservation Landmarks are eligible to use all of the historic preservation incentives in Subsection C. The incentives only apply within the boundary of the Historic Landmark or Conservation Landmark;

