2. Integrity. The resource has retained physical and associative features from the period of historic significance. For proposals to designate a Conservation Landmark or Conservation District, at least three of the following must be met. For proposals to designate a resource as a contributing resource in a Historic District or Conservation District, at least three of the following must be met. For proposals to designate a Historic Landmark or Historic District, at least four of the following must be met:

a. The resource remains in the exact location as during the period of historic significance;

b. The resource retains sufficient design elements to convey an association with the period of historic significance;

