An administrative change is a change to an element of a River Review that:

1. Is consistent with all conditions of the River Review approval;  
2. Meets all development standards not modified by the River Review;  
3. Does not change any quantity, dimension, or area identified in the approved plans or narrative other than disturbance area or a mitigation plan or narrative by more than 5 percent;  
4. Does not increase the approved temporary or permanent disturbance area;  
5. Does not decrease any quantity, dimension or area identified in an approved mitigation plan or narrative; and  
6. Does not result in additional tree removal.
